{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsKtBzvwAG3FKVqgRtt4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The forced-local trial is complete. **Verdict: UNDERDETERMINED** — format.md is not a sufficient behavioral specification of reference.py over these probes.\n\n**The two underdetermined behaviors the probes exercise:**\n\n1. **Entry ordering.** format.md never says in what order entries are serialized; reference.py sorts by key. Every multi-entry probe (indices 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7) admits more than one conforming output, and an insertion-order implementation visibly diverges on probes 1, 3, 4, 6, 7.\n2. **Backslash handling in values.** format.md mandates escaping only `;` and `=`, saying nothing about `\\` itself; reference.py doubles backslashes. This diverges on probes 3, 4, and 7.\n\nA third gap — reference.py escapes keys while format.md scopes escaping to values — exists in the text but is not exercised by any probe, so I documented it in resolution.json but kept it out of the findings, per E-A's scope. Divergent probe indices: **[1, 3, 4, 6, 7]**, with full per-probe reference-vs-independent outputs in result.json.\n\n**Evidence-requirement satisfiability in this run** (stated per requirement in resolution.json):\n\n- **E-A: satisfied at full strength.** It's an analytical claim over format.md and probes.json alone, checkable by any reader.\n- **E-B: not satisfiable at full strength.** It requires an implementer with no access to reference.py, but this session read reference.py at the mandatory observe-package node, and the CONTROL_ONLY configuration makes an isolated child architecturally unavailable. Best substitute: `independent_encode.py`, a format.md-literal implementation with the contamination declared in-file, hand-traced (no interpreter under Read+Write) but mechanically re-executable by the root verifier. Key robustness point: contamination can only bias a simulation *toward agreement* with reference.py — it can't manufacture divergence — so the observed divergence on 5 of 8 probes stands; only clean-room certification of the three agreement cases is lost.\n- **E-C: satisfied.** Both disjuncts of the verdict rule hold (multiple conforming outputs exist, and the traced implementation diverges), so UNDERDETERMINED follows.\n\n**Governance artifacts:** `decision.json` records DO_NOT_CREATE with `forced_control` noted, honestly stating that unforced, chi would have favored CREATE precisely because of E-B's isolation requirement (recorded as unresolved distinction Q1). `execution-ledger.jsonl` contains the five local-branch events in dependency order — observe-package, decide-topology (propose, `metadata.decision: \"DO_NOT_CREATE\"`, `forced_control: true`), local-resolve, self-check-local (pass, non-authoritative), return-local — with every capability-bearing file surfaced under a propose event at authoring time, no `complete` event, and no child-branch events. `child_invocations` is 0."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1198,"cache_read_input_tokens":66017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1198},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a50eda9f-03ae-4243-aabb-17c1e5a7da4e","uuid":"761ac660-4ec7-4e82-bc2f-980ffc1a1f6a","timestamp":"2026-08-09T14:24:01.582Z","request_id":"req_011CdsKtAtD6vNPgGCqyT6Yz"}
